  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance for Informed, Safe and Dignified Voluntary Returns of Vulnerable Migrants in Participating Countries of the Americas (WHA Regional AVR Program)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Program provides administrative, logistic, and financial support to migrants in vulnerable situations in the Western Hemisphere who are unable or do not want to remain in host countries to return to their origin countries in Central and South America and the Caribbean. The program is based on IOM&#x2019;s Return, Readmission and Reintegration (RRR) Policy. The key outcomes of the new phase of the program, contemplated for the period of 01 May 2023 &#x2013; 30 April 2024, are the following: (1) Migrants in vulnerable situations in need of voluntary return support are able to make an informed decision on return; and, (2) More migrants in the region voluntarily return to countries of origin in a safe, orderly, efficient, humane, and dignified manner. Basic humanitarian assistance for program participants is critical to ensure that returnees avoid negative humanitarian outcomes and protection risks. IOM foresees a continuation of basic support upon arrival, in line with previous program iterations, to continue to ensure that return is indeed safe and dignified.</narrative>
  </description>
